{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Sally goes on a Safari"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "In Case of Rain"}, {"type": "position", "content": 10}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 8}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Describe characteristics of different people and their jobs."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations"}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations"}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations"}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations"}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations"}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations"}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le08ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The First Conditional "}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You can use the first conditional to talk about actions and situations in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are two parts to the sentence. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "One part is the <span class =\"strong\">condition</span>. The other part is the <span class =\"strong\">result</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Form:<br /><span class=\"italic\"> If + subject + Simple Present tense  + subject + will/won't</span><br /> You use a comma after the condition in this form. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can flip the two parts of the sentence so that the result comes first. It can be in interrogative form. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Form:<br /><span class=\"italic\"> Will/Won't + subject + if + subject + Simple Present tense  ?</span><br/><br/> You can also use the future time clauses <span class=\"italic\">when</span> and  <span class=\"italic\">after</span> in the condition."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\"> Condition </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Result</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">After it rains, </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> we will go inside. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> If we leave at 4 p.m. sharp,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">we'll get to the camp by 9 p.m</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Result </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Condition</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Will we visit the museum </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> when we have time? </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> We will make pit stops along the way</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> if the weather isn't too bad.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Quantifiers "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use a quantifier before a noun to indicate the amount or number of an item."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use quantifiers with both count and non-count nouns."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use all of the quantifiers below with both count and non-count nouns."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\"> Quantifier </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Meaning</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more<br /> less/fewer<br /> no/none<br /> any /not any<br /> some<br /> a lot of / lots of<br /> plenty of<br /> enough\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a larger number/amount<br /> a smaller number/amount<br /> 0<br /> to ask about / say there none<br /> a small number/amount<br /> a very large number/amount<br /> more than you need<br /> as much as you need\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I hope there's no rain tomorrow."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We had plenty of rain this whole week!"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "nature reserve"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an area of land where wild animals and plants are protected  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We can go to the nature reserve."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le08ob10aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about things to do on a trip."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "double-decker bus"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a bus with two levels "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We are taking a tour of the city on the double-decker bus."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le08ob10aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Sweet."}, {"type": "definition", "content": "great; excellent"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sweet. I hope we can go tomorrow."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le08ob10aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "museum "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a building where important objects are kept and open to the public "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I want to go to the city museum."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le08ob10aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hike"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a long walk in the mountains"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The safari includes a hike to the mountains."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le08ob10aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word